# Build context exclusions for the backend image (context: ./backend).
#
# The backend Dockerfile was written to be built from `backend/`, so the container build
# needs its own ignore file; the repository-root `.dockerignore` only applies to contexts
# rooted at the repository.
#
# `.venv` matters most here: a worktree-local virtualenv may be a junction pointing at
# another checkout, and sending it as build context is both slow and a way to bake a
# developer's local state into an image.
.venv
venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache
.mypy_cache
.ruff_cache
htmlcov
.coverage
tests
data/receipts
data/samples
.local-storage
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
